Hullo,

I have actually found the sources for the original Hack v1.0, as
distributed with SunOS 4.x and earlier. This version is dated
Jul-1985, man that was a long time ago! (even for me)

ftp://ftp.uu.net/pub/games

So what you say? I liked the old version for its simplicity and
quickness of game (mostly!), but I haven't played it since '94. By
then our stingey sysadmins considered the game a waste of disk and
bandwidth, and uninstalled it (go figure).

Lo, after much scrounging over the net I found and quickly snarfed the
original source.

Boy the code is really horrible in places, think "Story of Mel" (well
maybe not that bad). There were a lot of bugs which needed fixing just
to get the thing to compile, probably a result of earlier "features"
in cc which were fixed in later versions.

But after perseverence I managed to get the thing to compile, and then
run, under Solaris 2.8. However, the game still core dumps at certain
points.

So I was wondering if anyone has/seen a port to Solaris ????

If not, that's ok, I will take on this project as an intellectual
exercise, slowly rising to an obsession  :-p

